==Strategy==
Ranged and Long-Ranged attackers are your friends here. [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] may be of use for fending off the Master A., and [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] can take care of Camelle and any other Brollows that break through your line. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can be used to stall the Camelle and Master A. if well-protected. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is good for getting a hit or two on Master A., but timing is very important. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is great here for taking down the hordes of peons while dealing occasional chip damage to Camelle and Master A. Other rushers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] should be phenomenal for sneaking hits in against the stage's bosses. If you're playing on 4 Crown, a good way to regain ground in the second phase is [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]], as it's guaranteed to knockback the enemy at the front, since none of the enemies can crit.

For higher crown difficulties, you can use units with [[Wave Attack]]s like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs Cat]] to deal with the constant Brollows as well as damage the backliners and oncoming peons.

A sufficiently leveled [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] can one-shot the Brollows with full anti-Floating Treasures at level 60 for {{4c}}, but you can use [[Cat Combo]]s to make up the level gap. Even then, this cat can be extremely useful in this stage, as they still deal good damage even if they don't instantly kill the Brollows.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]], [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]], and [[Splendid Ganesha (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganesha]] are great units to bring should you have them, as they outrange Camelle and can snipe the Brollows provided a proper defense.
*Tankers like [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] or [[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Hades]], etc., are able to sponge hits from the Brollows & Camelle without much trouble while providing a stepping-stone for your LD/Wave units.

